Windows: a 248-character path gets the long-path prefix

osl_getSystemPathFromFileURL left paths of up to MAX_PATH - 12 (248)
characters without the \\?\ prefix. CreateDirectoryW without it takes
at most 247 characters (its documented MAX_PATH - 12 counts the
terminating null), so a
folder whose path is exactly 248 characters failed with error 206,
ERROR_FILENAME_EXCED_RANGE. The extension manager makes folders 86 to
99 characters below the user profile (user\extensions\tmp\registry\...,
user\uno_packages\cache\...); with a profile path of 149 to about 162
characters one of them landed on 248, dp_misc::create_folder threw, and
the exception left LOK's start-up uncaught (Ely R15.33). Shorter and
longer profiles started. Prefix paths from 248 characters on.

GetLongPathNameW and FindFirstFileW take 259 characters without the
prefix, so the MAX_PATH checks before them stay as they are.

diff --git a/sal/osl/w32/file_url.cxx b/sal/osl/w32/file_url.cxx
index ea90ccad7..21b4fc827 100644
--- a/sal/osl/w32/file_url.cxx
+++ b/sal/osl/w32/file_url.cxx
@@ -684,14 +684,14 @@ oslFileError osl_getSystemPathFromFileURL_(const OUString& strURL, rtl_uString *
             else
             {
                 /* do not separate the directory and file case, so the maximal path length without prefix is MAX_PATH-12 */
-                if ( nDecodedLen - nSkip <= MAX_PATH - 12 )
+                if ( nDecodedLen - nSkip < MAX_PATH - 12 )
                 {
                     sTempPath = sDecodedURL->subView(nSkip);
                 }
                 else
                 {
                     sDecodedURL = GetCaseCorrectPathName(sDecodedURL->subView(nSkip));
-                    if (sDecodedURL->getLength() <= MAX_PATH - 12
+                    if (sDecodedURL->getLength() < MAX_PATH - 12
                         || sDecodedURL->startsWith(WSTR_SYSTEM_ROOT_PATH)
                         || sDecodedURL->startsWith(WSTR_LONG_PATH_PREFIX))
                     {
